# Normalise line endings, because this repository hashes its own source documents.
#
# GEOMETRY-CONTROL.md is hashed into every build output, and a regression test (STT-012) fails when
# the parts manifest was built from a different hash. That is a deliberate guard against editing the
# control document and forgetting to rebuild.
#
# Without this file, Git's autocrlf gives a Windows checkout CRLF line endings while the committed
# blob and every Linux checkout keep LF. The same document then hashes two different ways, so the
# provenance recorded by a local build and by CI disagree for a reason that has nothing to do with
# the geometry. Forcing LF in the working tree makes the hash a property of the content alone.
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts must never be line-ending converted; doing so corrupts them.
*.glb binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary

# Hash manifests are compared byte-for-byte by the viewer drift check.
*.sha256 text eol=lf
